{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And if she is purified of her flux.</b> That is, when the zav is purified of his flux, <b>and she shall count for herself seven days</b>, as the zav counts, of whom it is written וספר לו שבעת ימים לטהרתו, <b>and afterward she shall be purified</b>, like the purification of the zav. And from this it would appear that she requires immersion in living water, as is the rule for the zav, of whom it is written ורחץ בשרו במים חיים וטהר." "<b>But</b> the intent of our Rabbis of blessed memory is that the verse ואחר תטהר comes to include for her a [special] purification, for there was no need to write ואחר תטהר, since the woman is surely included within the man. And since it was necessary to write ואחר תטהר, it adds for her a purification — that is, to be lenient in the purification of the zavah, that she may purify herself in the waters of a mikveh in the manner of all others who become purified in the Torah, and need not require living water." "<b>And she shall count for herself seven days.</b> She is not required to recite a blessing over this counting as over the counting of the omer, for over all commandments one recites a blessing before their performance, but this one — if she sees [blood] within the seven, she undoes what she has counted retroactively, and the blessing would turn out to be in vain. For this reason it is impossible for her to recite a blessing over this commandment." "<b>And the reason</b> for this commandment that was given to the woman is what our Rabbis of blessed memory said in the Midrash: she shed the blood of man, therefore her blood shall be shed. And thus it is written (Genesis 9): שופך דם האדם באדם דמו ישפך. And likewise with challah and the kindling of the lamp: she contaminated the challah of the world and extinguished the lamp of the world; therefore she shall guard the challah and kindle the lamp on the Sabbath."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:37.155022042Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}